# Local scratch tools that have never been part of this repository.
#
# 🚨 AN EXPLICIT LIST, NOT A BLANKET `*`. On `flow-local-path` this file was a
# single `*` with per-extension re-includes, and it silently hid three things
# that belonged in the repo: the swiftcheck harness itself, the log scorers, and
# the harness's own run.sh. A file that is simply ABSENT from a fresh clone is
# invisible to every local check, so the ignore rule names exactly what it hides
# and nothing else.
#
# `swiftcheck/` is deliberately NOT here: it is tracked, and `run.sh` refuses to
# run if any of its inputs — itself included — is missing from the index.
#
# 🚨 2026-08-18: `turn_srtp_test/` LEFT this list, and the reason is the one this
# header already warns about — it stopped being a scratch tool. It is the load
# generator for the N=60 blackhole investigation, and it took three correctness
# fixes (a barrier that was not one, a worker that could hang forever inside
# Write, and an arm whose label could not be checked against the wire) that would
# otherwise have lived on one laptop. Only its SOURCE is tracked; the binary
# built beside it stays ignored.
# Its sink, `turn_srtp_server/`, followed the same day and for the same reason:
# the generator and the sink are ONE system, and half of it in the repo is the
# failure this header describes, just slower. Its source is UNCHANGED by that
# move — only its visibility. Both binaries stay ignored.

apppass_test/
captcha_test/
cookie_test/
logscore/
rtpopus_interop/
turn_bw_server/
turn_bw_test/
turn_quota_test/
turn_srtp_server/turn_srtp_server
turn_srtp_test/turn_srtp_test
wrapa_test/
